WEBVTT

00:01.360 --> 00:04.272
- Thank you for a lovely dinner.
- You're welcome.

00:08.440 --> 00:11.193
- Good night.
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:11.360 --> 00:13.669
Are you sure
you don't want me to tuck you in?

00:13.840 --> 00:15.956
I don't need to be tucked, Charlie.

00:16.120 --> 00:19.635
Oh, come on, everybody needs
a good tucking once in a while.

00:19.800 --> 00:22.712
Well, then, go tuck yourself.

00:22.880 --> 00:24.757
I guess I'll have to.

00:27.880 --> 00:30.917
I'm not saying no.
I'm just saying not now.

00:31.400 --> 00:32.435
I understand.

00:32.840 --> 00:35.070
- Good night.
- Good night.

00:38.360 --> 00:39.634
How about now?

00:40.520 --> 00:42.033
Funny.

00:44.600 --> 00:46.795
I wasn't going for a laugh.

00:50.640 --> 00:51.629
Come on, Luther.

00:54.800 --> 00:56.279
Rose?

00:57.120 --> 00:59.475
No, it couldn't be.

01:00.360 --> 01:03.750
I'm so backed up I'm literally cockeyed.

01:13.360 --> 01:15.510
Hot girl at 12 o'clock.

01:18.720 --> 01:21.678
- Where?
- Over there.

01:24.560 --> 01:26.790
That would be 9 o'clock.

01:26.960 --> 01:30.157
No, it's 12. Actually, 12:05.

01:30.320 --> 01:31.594
Twelve-ish.

01:33.120 --> 01:35.953
- Wanna straighten him out or should I?
- Go ahead, take a swing.

01:36.120 --> 01:40.272
Okay. The reason guys say
hot girl at like 12 o'clock or 3 o'clock...

01:40.440 --> 01:43.989
...is to specify a location
using the clock face as kind of a map.

01:44.160 --> 01:45.832
What if you have a digital watch?

01:47.200 --> 01:50.476
First of all, you're not gonna meet
any women if you wear a digital watch.

01:50.640 --> 01:53.438
Second of all, it doesn't matter.
The clock face is imaginary.

01:53.600 --> 01:55.591
How do you know
what time you saw the girl?

01:56.720 --> 01:58.199
Oh, my God.

01:58.360 --> 02:02.478
You know what? I'm wrong.
There's a hot girl and it's 12:06.

02:02.960 --> 02:04.234
Check.

02:05.680 --> 02:09.673
Hey, he likes girls and he can tell time.
I'm a happy dad.

02:14.680 --> 02:16.796
- Hello, Your Honor, what's up?
- Your Honor?

02:16.960 --> 02:19.599
Oh, your uncle's dating a judge.

02:19.760 --> 02:21.990
This weekend? Sure, that sounds great.

02:22.360 --> 02:25.511
- You mean like an &lt;i>American Idol&lt;/i> judge?
- No, a real judge.

02:25.680 --> 02:28.069
&lt;i>American Idol&lt;/i> judges are real, Dad.

02:29.760 --> 02:31.955
So, what,
we'd be staying in adjoining rooms?

02:32.120 --> 02:34.714
- No, no, no, one room is fine.
- Why is he dating a judge?

02:34.880 --> 02:36.871
- Is he trying to get out of something?
- No.

02:37.040 --> 02:39.110
More like he's trying
to get into something.

02:39.280 --> 02:40.713
Good one.

02:40.880 --> 02:42.711
- You understood that?
- Not really.

02:42.880 --> 02:44.313
That's how I knew it was good.

02:44.480 --> 02:48.268
Oh, yeah, that's a very romantic hotel.
I've stayed there...

02:48.440 --> 02:52.274
Never in my life.
Right. Okay, talk to you later.

02:53.840 --> 02:56.877
Santa Barbara, this weekend, one room.

02:57.040 --> 02:58.996
Oh, now I get it.

02:59.520 --> 03:01.829
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

03:04.600 --> 03:06.511
- Son of a gun, Alan, look.
- What?

03:06.680 --> 03:07.908
- The blond.
- Where?

03:08.080 --> 03:09.877
Twelve-oh-eight.

03:11.000 --> 03:12.069
She looks like Rose.

03:12.240 --> 03:14.310
It couldn't be.
She's still in England, right?

03:14.960 --> 03:17.997
- Last I heard.
- I got a postcard from her the other day.

03:18.480 --> 03:20.675
- Really? What did it say?
- Well, let's see.

03:20.840 --> 03:25.675
"Dear Jake, how are you? I am fine.
Hope you're doing well in school."

03:25.840 --> 03:28.798
I think that's a joke because she knows
I struggle with my grades.

03:28.960 --> 03:32.794
Let's see, what else? Oh, yeah.
"Say hello from England to everybody."

03:33.400 --> 03:34.799
Hello from England.

03:36.080 --> 03:38.036
Well, there you go. She's in England.

03:38.520 --> 03:41.512
I guess.
So why do I keep thinking I see her?

03:41.680 --> 03:44.478
- Maybe you miss her.
- I don't think so.

03:44.640 --> 03:47.313
I was a little down when she left,
which is to be expected...

03:47.480 --> 03:49.516
...but I've got Linda now
and I've moved on...

03:49.680 --> 03:51.636
...and why am I talking to you
about my life?

03:51.800 --> 03:53.028
Because I'm a good listener?

03:55.400 --> 03:57.675
Because you have no other friends?

04:01.200 --> 04:03.430
- We're dropping him off at his mother's?
- Yep.

04:28.080 --> 04:31.959
&lt;i>Dear Charlie,&lt;/i>
&lt;i>greetings from faggy old London.&lt;/i>

04:35.840 --> 04:38.638
&lt;i>Greetings from foggy old London.&lt;/i>

04:39.360 --> 04:42.796
&lt;i>Hope you are doing well&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and not working too hard.&lt;/i>

04:42.960 --> 04:44.393
&lt;i>Things are going great for me.&lt;/i>

04:44.560 --> 04:47.518
&lt;i>I love my job and my flat&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and my new friends.&lt;/i>

04:47.680 --> 04:50.513
&lt;i>Sometimes, my life in Malibu&lt;/i>
&lt;i>feels like a crazy dream.&lt;/i>

04:50.960 --> 04:53.428
&lt;i>I hope you can forgive me&lt;/i>
&lt;i>for all my bizarre behavior...&lt;/i>

04:53.600 --> 04:55.955
&lt;i>... and know that I will always&lt;/i>
&lt;i>remember you fondly.&lt;/i>

04:56.120 --> 04:58.111
&lt;i>Your friend, Rose.&lt;/i>

04:58.280 --> 05:00.157
&lt;i>P.S., Give my best to Alan.&lt;/i>

05:00.320 --> 05:03.357
&lt;i>I'm sure by now&lt;/i>
&lt;i>he's found a place of his own.&lt;/i>

05:05.200 --> 05:08.317
- What you got there?
- It's a letter from Rose.

05:08.480 --> 05:10.311
Really? That come today?

05:10.480 --> 05:13.552
No, a few months ago.
I just never got around to reading it.

05:14.000 --> 05:16.434
I noticed you didn't toss it out.

05:17.320 --> 05:19.197
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Charlie.

05:19.360 --> 05:20.952
Of all the broads who've staggered...

05:21.120 --> 05:23.156
...bare-assed
through these hallowed halls...

05:23.320 --> 05:25.197
...she's the one who really got to you.

05:25.720 --> 05:27.517
Yeah, she got to me.

05:27.680 --> 05:31.639
She put a sleeping pill in my Scotch
and superglued my testicles to my leg.

05:32.040 --> 05:33.871
You just can't get past that, can you?

05:34.880 --> 05:36.074
Well, it doesn't matter.

05:36.240 --> 05:38.834
I'm in a real relationship now
with an incredible woman.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.991
A judge, a constitutional scholar.

05:41.160 --> 05:43.037
A woman who may one day
be a state senator.

05:43.440 --> 05:45.510
But does she care enough
to line her mittens...

05:45.680 --> 05:48.069
...with hair she collects
from your shower drain?

05:48.560 --> 05:50.357
I don't know yet. We're going slow.

05:50.760 --> 05:52.478
- Really?
- Yes.

05:52.640 --> 05:55.438
Getting to know each other as people
before we jump into bed...

05:55.600 --> 05:58.558
...and get to know each other
as, you know, animals.

05:58.720 --> 06:01.280
Just do me a favor
and make the first time at her place...

06:01.440 --> 06:04.512
...because you're gonna spring forth
like a Water Wiggle.

07:21.680 --> 07:22.829
&lt;i>Charlie?&lt;/i>

07:23.000 --> 07:24.558
- Charlie?
- What?

07:28.400 --> 07:29.833
I need your help.

07:30.360 --> 07:34.239
If you're doing laundry,
all I can say is you're doing it wrong.

07:34.720 --> 07:38.474
No, no, the lady I've been seeing,
you know, Linda's friend Donna?

07:38.640 --> 07:41.552
She wants to... How shall we say?

07:41.720 --> 07:43.278
Take it up a notch.

07:43.720 --> 07:46.712
- Yeah, so?
- I'm out of notches.

07:47.520 --> 07:50.876
- What do you need?
- A younger man's penis.

07:52.280 --> 07:55.352
My night stand, top drawer,
next to the Ping-Pong paddle.

07:55.520 --> 07:57.670
Take one with water
and stall for 20 minutes.

07:57.840 --> 07:58.829
Thanks.

07:59.000 --> 08:00.877
- Alan?
- Yeah?

08:01.040 --> 08:03.270
- Don't those hurt?
- Hell, yeah.

08:03.440 --> 08:06.477
- Why don't you take them off?
- There's a penalty involved.

08:08.120 --> 08:09.838
Long story.

08:11.760 --> 08:14.354
I can tell you how it ends.

08:21.240 --> 08:25.438
- Lovely dinner.
- Yeah. Food was great.

08:25.760 --> 08:30.470
- It's a beautiful room.
- Yeah. Room's great.

08:31.680 --> 08:33.318
Nice view.

08:34.160 --> 08:36.276
Yep, view's great.

08:46.320 --> 08:48.276
Oh, for God's sake.

08:48.440 --> 08:50.715
- Who is it?
- Room service, señor.

08:51.440 --> 08:52.873
We didn't order anything.

08:53.040 --> 08:56.191
It's champagne.
Compliments of the hotel.

08:56.720 --> 08:59.632
- Can you slip it under the door?
- Charlie.

09:01.200 --> 09:03.760
Don't move. Don't change your mind.

09:12.720 --> 09:14.870
- Do you want I open?
- No, thank you.

09:15.280 --> 09:17.191
Okay, good night.

09:30.200 --> 09:31.189
Charlie.

09:32.080 --> 09:35.072
- Yeah?
- I'm waiting.

09:35.440 --> 09:36.873
For what?

09:37.840 --> 09:39.512
Oh, right.

09:41.120 --> 09:42.678
Hang on.

09:47.040 --> 09:49.110
What are you doing to the rose?

09:49.400 --> 09:52.119
I just don't want it looking at me.

10:04.560 --> 10:07.472
- Anything interesting going on in school?
- I started algebra.

10:07.640 --> 10:08.755
Oh, how's that going?

10:08.920 --> 10:11.957
I don't get it at all,
but the teacher's really hot.

10:13.200 --> 10:17.193
- Well, that's nice.
- Yeah, she's got some really great racks.

10:18.800 --> 10:20.358
I think you mean rack.

10:20.520 --> 10:22.988
No, she's got two,
and they're ginormous.

10:25.240 --> 10:28.118
It's kind of cool
that she's teaching algebra.

10:30.680 --> 10:32.272
Nothing?

10:32.760 --> 10:34.751
Boy, that killed in detention.

10:35.160 --> 10:39.312
- Oh, hey, how was Santa Barbara?
- Santa Bar-bra?

10:40.760 --> 10:43.991
It's Spanish for "City of Great Racks."

10:44.520 --> 10:46.829
Alan,
I got no patience for your kid today.

10:47.200 --> 10:48.315
Go do your homework.

10:48.480 --> 10:51.074
Oh, right. I have
a big reading ass-ignment.

10:54.680 --> 10:55.954
You're not my audience.

11:00.760 --> 11:04.070
- Remember when he was cute?
- The memory is fading.

11:04.240 --> 11:06.708
So how was your big night with Linda?

11:07.320 --> 11:09.880
- Fine.
- Just fine?

11:10.040 --> 11:13.157
Yes. Just fine.

11:13.320 --> 11:16.551
Oh, I see.

11:17.320 --> 11:20.278
No, you don't.

11:20.440 --> 11:22.351
All right.

11:23.120 --> 11:27.318
- Wanna talk about it?
- Oh, golly, Alan, more than anything.

11:27.920 --> 11:30.354
Okay, never mind. Stew in it.

11:30.520 --> 11:32.078
Thank you.

11:38.680 --> 11:42.753
I finally got to step up to the plate
and I was swinging a garden hose.

11:47.480 --> 11:49.232
You happy?

11:49.400 --> 11:51.311
Well, I'm not sad.

11:53.400 --> 11:55.311
What do you think the problem was?

11:58.120 --> 11:59.473
I saw her again.

11:59.640 --> 12:01.278
- Saw who?
- Rose.

12:01.440 --> 12:03.237
She brought champagne
to our hotel room...

12:03.400 --> 12:05.277
...except this time, she was Hispanic.

12:08.040 --> 12:09.393
What was she last time?

12:09.560 --> 12:11.232
Last time, she was a blond with coffee...

12:11.400 --> 12:13.391
...and before that,
she was a redhead with a dog.

12:13.560 --> 12:15.949
- What kind of dog?
- What difference does it make?

12:17.200 --> 12:18.679
I like dogs.

12:20.160 --> 12:21.149
Go on.

12:21.320 --> 12:24.118
If I didn't know any better,
I'd say she was stalking me again.

12:24.280 --> 12:26.999
- From England?
- We don't know she's in England.

12:27.160 --> 12:29.833
She sends letters and postcards.
Jake gets them all the time.

12:30.000 --> 12:33.709
Like she couldn't leave a stack of them
with some friend to mail every few days.

12:34.200 --> 12:37.715
Oh, wow, are you listening to yourself?
Even Rose isn't that crazy.

12:37.880 --> 12:40.440
Oh, and she's gonna fly back and forth
with a dog?

12:40.600 --> 12:43.319
She could hire a local dog.

12:45.080 --> 12:47.389
Charlie, Rose is in England.
She's not stalking you.

12:47.560 --> 12:50.472
And whatever you think you're seeing
is in your head.

12:52.320 --> 12:53.878
Yeah, you're probably right.

12:55.400 --> 12:59.188
Regardless,
last night was less than a triumph.

12:59.840 --> 13:02.434
Why didn't you just take
one of your pills?

13:02.600 --> 13:06.513
Because somebody else
took my last three.

13:07.680 --> 13:09.398
Oh, yeah.

13:09.880 --> 13:11.393
Thank you.

13:13.000 --> 13:15.116
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

13:16.040 --> 13:17.075
That's four.

13:17.960 --> 13:19.632
The first one was a twofer.

13:23.000 --> 13:25.389
- What kind of dog?
- I don't know, it was a dog.

13:26.720 --> 13:30.235
Four legs and a tail.
Can we please get back to my problem?

13:30.400 --> 13:32.709
Not a dog person.

13:33.640 --> 13:36.279
So you believe
you're seeing people who aren't there?

13:36.440 --> 13:37.509
No, no, no.

13:37.680 --> 13:39.875
They're there,
but they're not who they are.

13:40.040 --> 13:41.393
Well, then, who are they?

13:41.560 --> 13:44.916
I don't know who they are,
but they all look like Rose.

13:45.080 --> 13:48.755
- Your stalker.
- Well, that's kind of harsh.

13:48.920 --> 13:50.672
You told me she broke into your home...

13:50.840 --> 13:53.957
...disrobed and handcuffed herself
to your refrigerator.

13:54.600 --> 13:56.431
Just the one time.

13:57.800 --> 14:00.997
So why do I keep seeing her
everywhere I go?

14:01.160 --> 14:04.914
Well, Charlie, if I tell you that now,
what'll we do for the rest of the hour?

14:06.080 --> 14:07.308
I'm joshing.

14:10.120 --> 14:12.270
Why don't we talk
about your current relationship?

14:12.440 --> 14:15.637
Linda? Well, let's see.
She's a municipal-court judge.

14:15.800 --> 14:17.870
- Very impressive.
- Thank you.

14:18.040 --> 14:19.314
I meant for her, Charlie.

14:20.680 --> 14:22.557
It's hardly your accomplishment now,
is it?

14:23.000 --> 14:26.072
Well, yeah, in a way.
I've never done a judge before.

14:26.240 --> 14:29.312
Well, from what you told me,
you still haven't.

14:31.040 --> 14:32.268
Touché.

14:32.760 --> 14:34.830
Pays to listen.

14:35.000 --> 14:37.719
- So how old is Linda?
- She's about my age.

14:37.880 --> 14:40.110
First time you've been
with a woman that old?

14:40.280 --> 14:41.759
Oh, no, not at all.

14:41.920 --> 14:44.434
So you've had age-appropriate
relationships before?

14:44.600 --> 14:47.319
Relationships? No, no, are you crazy?

14:47.480 --> 14:50.278
Am I crazy? Pot, kettle, Charlie.

14:50.960 --> 14:54.270
Okay, look, I didn't come to therapy
to talk this to death.

14:55.720 --> 14:59.759
I've seen Rose three times
and it's ruining my sex life with Linda.

14:59.920 --> 15:03.515
Can you help me or do I have to learn
to shoot pool with a rope?

15:04.080 --> 15:05.957
Well, thank you
for that disturbing image.

15:08.280 --> 15:10.510
Best I can tell,
for the first time in your life...

15:10.680 --> 15:12.910
...you are involved
in an adult relationship.

15:13.080 --> 15:15.958
It's challenging,
maybe even a little intimidating.

15:16.120 --> 15:19.032
And the fact that you're fantasizing
about a woman in England...

15:19.200 --> 15:22.033
...who idolized you
beyond all rational measure...

15:22.200 --> 15:24.794
...well, that tells me
that you're afraid to grow up.

15:24.960 --> 15:26.996
And we call that
the Peter Pan syndrome.

15:28.840 --> 15:30.671
That's pretty good.

15:31.120 --> 15:34.908
So, what can we do,
you know, Peter-wise?

15:35.080 --> 15:38.277
If you're committed to personal growth,
you'll walk through your fear...

15:38.440 --> 15:41.876
...and embrace the challenges
of a really meaningful relationship...

15:42.040 --> 15:43.314
...with an adult woman.

15:43.840 --> 15:46.912
And your only other choice
is to live the emotionally stunted life...

15:47.080 --> 15:49.548
...you've been living over and over.

15:49.720 --> 15:52.359
Never growing, never changing.

15:55.240 --> 15:58.710
&lt;i>Good afternoon, and welcome aboard&lt;/i>
&lt;i>British Airways Flight 471...&lt;/i>

15:58.880 --> 16:01.474
&lt;i>... nonstop&lt;/i>
&lt;i>to London 's Heathrow Airport.&lt;/i>

16:21.080 --> 16:22.752
Charlie.

16:22.920 --> 16:24.273
Surprise.

16:25.840 --> 16:27.478
What are you doing here?

16:28.120 --> 16:29.872
I'm not sure. I just needed to see you.

16:30.040 --> 16:32.918
I need to talk to you. I can
come back if now is not a good time.

16:33.080 --> 16:34.752
No, no, it's okay.

16:35.360 --> 16:38.432
I know you've probably moved on.
I thought I had too...

16:38.600 --> 16:42.354
...but everywhere I look,
I keep seeing your face...

16:42.520 --> 16:45.910
...so I started thinking, maybe...

16:47.320 --> 16:49.276
I don't know what I'm thinking.
Are you busy?

16:49.440 --> 16:51.874
Can I take you out
for a cold beer or something?

16:52.040 --> 16:55.794
Actually, on this side of the pond,
we drink our beer warm.

16:56.640 --> 16:58.198
You can still catch a buzz, right?

16:58.960 --> 17:01.428
- Oh, yeah.
- Then warm's fine.

17:01.600 --> 17:02.589
Okay.

17:02.760 --> 17:05.797
- Well, I'll just get my purse.
- Great.

17:16.400 --> 17:18.197
So I'm not screwing up
any plans of yours?

17:18.360 --> 17:21.955
Oh, no. This fits perfectly into my plans.

17:27.480 --> 17:29.391
- Oh, Linda, hi.
- Hi, Alan.

17:29.560 --> 17:33.075
I'm sorry to show up unannounced, but
Charlie hasn't been answering his phone.

17:33.240 --> 17:34.912
And I wanted to make sure he's okay.

17:35.080 --> 17:38.038
Oh, Charlie's fine.
We have a pharmacy that delivers.

17:38.520 --> 17:40.033
What?

17:40.600 --> 17:43.478
- Nothing, nothing. Come on in.
- Thanks.

17:43.640 --> 17:46.313
He should be getting up
sometime soon, anyway.

17:46.480 --> 17:48.391
So how are things with you and Donna?

17:48.560 --> 17:50.357
Good, good.

17:51.000 --> 17:52.274
I'll go get Charlie.

17:52.440 --> 17:54.908
Hey, Dad, girls' volleyball.
Lot of bouncing boobs.

17:55.080 --> 17:57.036
- Not now, Jake.
- You told me to tell you.

17:57.200 --> 17:58.269
- I didn't.
- Yes, you did.

17:58.440 --> 17:59.873
Shut up.

18:01.400 --> 18:02.594
Oh, hey.

18:02.760 --> 18:05.320
- Hello. You must be Jake.
- Yeah, who are you?

18:05.480 --> 18:07.471
Linda.
I'm a friend of your Uncle Charlie's.

18:07.640 --> 18:08.993
Are you the judge?

18:09.160 --> 18:11.879
- Do you play volleyball?
- No. Do you?

18:12.040 --> 18:14.076
No, I just like to watch them
jump up and down.

18:14.240 --> 18:17.516
Okay. Heigh-ho, go away.

18:17.880 --> 18:21.156
I thought Charlie was asleep,
but he's not in his room.

18:21.320 --> 18:22.594
Berta, have you seen Charlie?

18:22.760 --> 18:24.034
- He's not in his bed?
- No.

18:24.200 --> 18:25.952
- Passed out on the bathroom floor?
- No.

18:26.120 --> 18:28.509
- Rubbing oil on the volleyball girls?
- No.

18:32.200 --> 18:35.078
Well, that just leaves the bars,
hospitals and jails.

18:36.240 --> 18:37.514
I'll go get the yellow pages.

18:39.360 --> 18:41.476
Well, he couldn't have gone very far.

18:41.640 --> 18:43.870
Hey, Dad. Hot girl in a thong.

18:44.040 --> 18:45.473
What time is it?

18:54.080 --> 18:55.399
Tepid.

18:56.760 --> 18:59.320
So London certainly agrees
with you, Rose.

18:59.480 --> 19:02.631
- You look beautiful.
- Thank you, Charlie.

19:02.800 --> 19:04.711
I just can't believe you're here.

19:04.880 --> 19:08.919
Yeah, well, I wanted you to know I've
been thinking a lot about you lately...

19:09.080 --> 19:11.310
...and I miss you.

19:11.680 --> 19:14.148
Oh, Charlie, I miss you too.

19:14.600 --> 19:16.113
Are you seeing anybody?

19:16.560 --> 19:21.953
Actually, I am seeing someone, but
I'm not really sure where it's going yet.

19:22.640 --> 19:24.631
- You?
- To be honest...

19:24.800 --> 19:26.870
...there is one lady I've been dating.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.598
She's actually my own age.

19:29.040 --> 19:31.474
- No.
- Yeah.

19:31.640 --> 19:34.712
But my therapist says
she's not good for me.

19:36.000 --> 19:38.036
And you think I am?

19:38.200 --> 19:42.478
Well, you've always loved me for
who I am instead of who I could be...

19:42.640 --> 19:45.200
...which is really wonderful,
because, let's face it...

19:45.360 --> 19:47.351
...we both love who I am.

19:50.080 --> 19:51.718
I do love you, Charlie.

19:52.200 --> 19:53.315
Great.

19:55.240 --> 19:56.275
So?

19:57.120 --> 19:58.917
So what?

19:59.280 --> 20:01.157
So, what's next?

20:02.080 --> 20:03.559
What do you mean?

20:04.440 --> 20:07.796
Well, you can't expect me to go back
to what we had without a commitment.

20:10.080 --> 20:12.036
- A commitment?
- Yes.

20:12.200 --> 20:13.713
I think we should get married.

20:16.080 --> 20:17.399
Married?

20:18.200 --> 20:19.553
Sell the house in Malibu...

20:19.720 --> 20:22.598
...and move to a kid-friendly
neighborhood here in London.

20:23.920 --> 20:25.558
Kid?

20:26.040 --> 20:27.678
Kids.

20:27.840 --> 20:30.195
We're gonna have kids, aren't we?

20:34.760 --> 20:38.070
&lt;i>Good afternoon and welcome aboard&lt;/i>
&lt;i>British Airways Flight 472...&lt;/i>

20:38.240 --> 20:41.869
&lt;i>... nonstop&lt;/i>
&lt;i>to Los Angeles International Airport.&lt;/i>

21:05.600 --> 21:07.591
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:07.760 --> 21:09.751
[ENGLISH]
